  userData: 'Built-in ImageGen. Create a single production sprite atlas texture for an original industrial warehouse game called Heavy Pockets. Wide canvas 4:3 aspect ratio, flat transparent alpha background. Exactly 4 columns by 3 rows, same square cell size, each cutout isolated and centered strictly on its own cell with thick transparent gutters. Invisible grid. Crisp semi-realistic painted 3D inventory renders, excellent silhouette, high contrast edges, warm copper and cool steel and faded amber accents, three-quarter orthographic, soft studio key from upper left, no drop shadows outside objects. Row 1 left to right: compact olive rectangular rugged electrical cargo module with latch; horizontal spool of shiny copper wire on a dark core; elongated ivory ceramic cartridge fuse with brass end caps horizontal; circular brass pressure gauge with ivory face and red needle. Row 2 left to right: translucent triangular glass optical prism with subtle refraction; polished steel annular ball bearing with clearly visible balls; rectangular orange handheld electronic multimeter with black dial, oriented landscape; ribbed dark teal cylindrical oil filter, lying horizontally. Row 3 left to right: compact amber signal beacon with protective wire cage; long slender steel industrial temperature probe with short attached cable, aligned horizontally; a hollow brushed titanium hexagonal shaft coupling; blank fully transparent cell. Exactly 11 individual objects in this precise arrangement. All objects complete, contained in the middle 65–75% of each cell, no cropped items, labels, borders, numbers, panels, letters or interface. Transparent background, not a checkerboard.'
